PAYTUNE — Complete Live Streaming Feature Plan
Live streaming should become one of PAYTUNE's major features, allowing African musicians, content creators, educators, churches, event organizers, businesses and media companies to broadcast live to audiences across Africa and internationally.

I recommend building it as a complete Live Studio + Live Viewer + Live Monetization + Live Management system.

The objective is not simply to add a button that starts a live video. PAYTUNE should support professional broadcasts, real-time audience interaction, revenue generation, moderation, event scheduling and recorded replays.
PAYTUNE LIVE
Broadcast live. Connect audiences. Build communities. Earn from your content.

(Live video) (Live audio) (Real-time chat) (Creator earnings)
1. Types of live streaming
PAYTUNE should support several broadcast formats.

1. Live video

Musicians, vloggers, journalists, influencers and other creators broadcast themselves using a camera, microphone or streaming software.
2. Live audio

Audio-only broadcasts, music sessions, radio shows, interviews, podcasts and discussions. Viewers can listen with lower bandwidth consumption.
3. Mobile vertical live

Portrait broadcasts for mobile-first audiences, with vertical chat and mobile-friendly controls.
4. Professional live production

Support OBS Studio and compatible broadcasting software through secure RTMP or SRT ingest, with multiple scenes, overlays and external cameras.
5. Live events and webinars

Training, conferences, education, product launches, interviews and online events with scheduled starting times and optional paid admission.
2. Creator Live Studio
Every eligible creator should have a dedicated Live Studio in their Artist or Creator Dashboard.
Before going live
Creators should be able to:
- Create a live broadcast title and description.
- Upload a live thumbnail or promotional poster.
- Select a category and language.
- Select the audience country or target region.
- Choose public, unlisted or private access.
- Choose free or paid admission.
- Schedule a broadcast for a future date.
- Enable or disable live chat.
- Enable audience participation and guest requests.
- Select video or audio-only mode.
- Select camera and microphone.
- Test microphone and camera before broadcasting.
- Select stream quality and latency mode.
- Configure recording and replay availability.
- Add moderators.
- Set age restrictions and content warnings.
- Set broadcast rights and music-use declarations.
During a live broadcast
Creators need a control room containing:
Feature	Function
Stream preview	See exactly what the audience receives
Live status	Display connection and broadcast health
Viewer count	Show current concurrent viewers
Live chat	Read and respond to audience messages
Moderation	Block, mute and remove inappropriate users
Stream quality	Monitor bitrate, frame rate and resolution
Microphone	Mute and unmute audio
Camera	Enable or disable video
Screen sharing	Share presentations or desktop
Scene controls	Switch between production scenes
Guest controls	Accept, reject and remove guests
End broadcast	Finish and close the live session


After the broadcast
The creator should receive:
- Total views and unique viewers.
- Peak concurrent viewers.
- Average watch duration.
- Total watch time.
- Viewer retention.
- Followers gained during the stream.
- Chat and interaction statistics.
- Eligible advertising revenue.
- Gifts, tips and paid access revenue.
- Processing status of the recording.
- Replay management and download options where permitted.
Important: a live session ending is not the same as a replay being ready. Recording, transcoding, moderation and publication must have their own verified processing states.
3. Live viewer experience
The audience should have a professional live watching experience.
Viewer features
1. Watch the broadcast in real time.
2. Change video quality when supported.
3. Switch to full-screen mode.
4. View live chat.
5. Send reactions and emojis.
6. Follow the creator.
7. Share the live stream.
8. Receive notifications when followed creators go live.
9. View the creator profile.
10. Report inappropriate broadcasts or messages.
11. Purchase paid access where applicable.
12. View the replay after the broadcast if the creator permits it.
Live chat
Chat should support:
- Text messages.
- Emoji and reactions.
- Creator announcements.
- Pinned messages.
- Moderator messages.
- Slow mode.
- Subscriber or paid-access-only chat where configured.
- Message deletion.
- User timeout and blocking.
- Spam and repeated-message detection.
- Language-aware moderation.
For African audiences, moderation must account for English, French, Portuguese, Arabic and African languages, including Kinyarwanda, Swahili, Hausa, Yoruba, Amharic and others. Automated moderation should support human review rather than automatically assuming every language is understood correctly.
4. Multi-guest live streaming
Allow creators to invite other people into a broadcast.

Features:
- Invite a guest using a private invitation link.
- Request to join a live session.
- Accept or reject guest requests.
- Host controls for removing guests.
- Multiple participant layouts.
- Individual microphone and camera controls.
- Guest connection quality monitoring.
- Guest permissions and consent.
- Recording of the broadcast, subject to participant consent.
I recommend launching with a host plus up to three guests, then expanding based on technical capacity.
5. Live monetization — how creators earn
This is particularly important for PAYTUNE.

Creators should have several ways to earn, while PAYTUNE earns from the platform services and eligible advertising.

A. Virtual gifts and tips

Viewers purchase digital gifts or send tips to creators. Show the gift animation during the broadcast and record the transaction in the creator's wallet.
B. Paid live events

Creators charge for admission to concerts, exclusive performances, masterclasses, conferences and special broadcasts.
C. Fan memberships

Support recurring memberships with exclusive live sessions, member badges and special community access. Membership billing must be separately implemented.
D. Sponsorships and direct advertising

Brands sponsor broadcasts, display approved advertisements or sponsor an event. PAYTUNE should manage advertiser contracts, campaign delivery and reporting.
E. Platform advertising

Eligible free live streams can display approved advertising. PAYTUNE earns advertising revenue and distributes the creator's eligible share according to its partner rules.
F. Merchandise and digital products

Creators can promote approved merchandise, music, digital products and other offerings during a broadcast.
