10. Security and paid-content protection
This is essential for a platform selling permanent access to content and paid live events.
- Never expose a creator's permanent stream key publicly.
- Give every creator a revocable, securely stored stream key.
- Authenticate and authorize every broadcast.
- Use short-lived playback tokens for private and paid streams.
- Check ticket purchases and entitlements on the backend.
- Prevent unauthorized direct access to paid stream playlists.
- Rate-limit chat, reactions and guest requests.
- Protect webhook endpoints with signature verification.
- Use idempotency for gifts, payments and refunds.
- Prevent duplicate gift transactions and duplicate ticket purchases.
- Encrypt sensitive secrets and protect financial records.
- Keep a complete audit trail.
- Prevent replay publication before processing and moderation checks are complete.
A signed playback URL alone is not a complete entitlement system. The backend must verify that the viewer is entitled to watch the actual event.
11. Responsive live experience across devices
The live system should adapt to the device without removing important capabilities.
Feature	Desktop	Tablet	Mobile
Broadcast studio	Full control room	Compact control room	Guided broadcast interface
Live player	Large landscape	Adaptive landscape	Portrait or landscape
