31. The most important PAYTUNE design principles
I recommend establishing these rules across the entire project:
1. African-first, globally accessible: Never hardcode Rwanda as the only country.
2. Mobile-first and responsive: Every important feature must work on Android, iOS, tablet and desktop.
3. Creator fairness: Explain monetization eligibility, earnings calculations and restrictions.
4. Financial accuracy: Every payment and payout must be traceable through a proper financial ledger.
5. Security first: Protect accounts, private media, paid content, financial records and administrative access.
6. Low-bandwidth support: Optimize uploads and playback for users with limited connectivity.
7. Real functionality: No fake views, fake earnings, simulated payments or misleading progress indicators.
8. Modular architecture: Each major feature should have its own maintainable backend and frontend modules.
9. Scalable infrastructure: Avoid architectural decisions that prevent expansion across African countries.
10. Legal readiness: Launch financial, advertising and content features only when their necessary legal and operational requirements are satisfied.
